# EXISTING QUICK ORDER BUILDER: CONTINUOUS BOUNDED IMPLEMENTATION

## Continue, do not restart

You are the existing Quick Order implementation owner, chat 01a10d78-0981-7150-9292-c5cde2730d4d, checkout 389a, branch codex/xenios-health-quick-order-20261005. Use GPT-6 Astra Ultra/highest available and disclose actual observed settings.

Your QO-P2-03/04 correction was already dispatched and acknowledged. Read this as a continuation addendum at a safe checkpoint. Do not reset, discard, duplicate or rebase away work in progress. First reconcile your current HEAD, dirty files, lease and task state against the coordinator.

Historical source anchor: f1e467f74b01ae2ab866bb791a3c11d657a5d69c, tree 6bc4fd7a7483822d4af87a3c07ab7263c0fbc377; handoff c807f1913ce95ebcf4113cd4f1ef5bdfb2f45d09.
Accepted base: 756a906877dbc174b7e228a259d2faa9c3af48ca.
Review: 324183e886af369a4ea27b9bf0f7b9c615b32139, docs 36 and 37 under docs/review/xenios-health-launch-review-20260930/.

Use the actual current successor if it has advanced. Preserve every prior receipt. Allowed placement does not waive task scope or protected-file rules.

## First delivery: both HTTP defects as one slice

Inside currently leased Quick Order modules, make containment and handler agree about namespace ownership and path interpretation. Read the real host normalization and Express configuration; do not invent a URL-normalization policy independently of the mounted application.

Cover:
- exact Quick Order namespace and descendants;
- case variations;
- duplicate leading slashes and the chosen interior-empty-segment policy;
- dot segments and encoded dot segments;
- backslashes;
- query and literal-fragment behavior;
- absolute-form request targets;
- malformed percent encoding and non-string/missing input where supported;
- near-prefix unrelated paths.

Separate two responsibilities:
1. Decide whether this module owns the effective target.
2. For owned targets, apply the strict path/body/session rules.

Unrelated malformed targets must not acquire a Quick Order JSON error merely because the handler is mounted at the root. Preserve next() exactly once where appropriate. Recognized Quick Order aliases must not escape containment through next(). A caller-provided host must never become trusted origin, actor, return URL or destination.

When disabled, recognized Quick Order API requests terminate before JSON/raw-body parsers retain the submitted body. For a future enabled handler, invalid owned targets remain refused under the canonical request contract. These are distinct test expectations, not one indiscriminate normalizer.

Use one consistent helper or derivation, in the existing allowed module scope. Keep .mjs runtime and TypeScript declaration surfaces coherent. Do not create files in the former forbidden locations. Do not weaken cases just to make the parser agree with the tests.

## Required regressions

Use the current real-loopback composition pattern with the actual-shape host normalizer and parser/verifier instrumentation.

Prove positive and negative controls:
- mixed-case and normalized Quick Order aliases are contained before parsing;
- //api/health/quick-order/requests cannot bypass refusal;
- dot-segment, backslash and encoded-dot cases preserve the boundary;
- //other and an absolute-form unrelated target pass to next();
- prefix lookalikes are not captured accidentally;
- relevant malformed owned inputs are refused, not routed elsewhere;
- an ordinary unrelated POST still reaches its expected parser;
- no accepted request creates a payment, external notification or durable intake.

Demonstrate the pre-fix failure and corrected behavior when the qualification slot permits. A miniature loopback composition is not full-App execution; label it precisely.

## Packet work in this slice

Within your own records/proposal scope:
- disclose the PWA install overlay and its separate HARD-file dependency;
- enumerate the missing mount/privacy regression cases;
- explain the App/server seam interaction with GATE-01;
- remove or source the unsupported 706 MiB figure;
- remove obsolete prefixes from your active lease only, retaining historical inventories and other owners;
- preserve the current six-file patch as unapproved and unapplied;
- if a permitted proposal edit changes its bytes, create a new explicit version and hash without inheriting old proposed-hash acceptance.

Do not silently add PwaLifecycle.tsx to A1. Do not widen isHealthGatewayPath: it remains exact /health. Keep a separate intake predicate for /health/quick-order. Source directory names must not change Health classification or legal applicability.

## What to do after this handoff

Freeze and push the source, then deliver one compact handoff to the existing coordinator through an authorized channel. A complete handoff is a checkpoint, not the end of the website project.

While the reviewer checks the immutable SHA, use only the next already-authorized non-conflicting task assigned by the coordinator. Useful candidates include the current mount regression specification, source-bound test harness improvements within your lease, proposal completeness and currentness-dependency documentation. Do not start another broad audit or keep generating records without a concrete outcome.

If a reviewer reports a defect, repair only the relevant cluster and rerun the affected tests. If an item requires missing authority, label that item BLOCKED and continue another lawful task. If no lawful source task remains, park honestly; do not code around a withheld permission.

## Conditional future implementation: only after actual authority

A1 is not approved. Until actual exact-baseline authority exists, do not apply the mount/privacy patch or change protected source. If approval arrives, verify all actual baselines, scope, leases and required regression pins, preserve disabled intake and submit the successor for exact-byte review. Successor-hash approval and manifest changes remain separate.

A2 is not approved. Do not draft new Quick Order SQL or persistence implementation under this addendum. If actual new-only source permission arrives, implement exactly the approved subset subject to doc 36 section 7. In particular:
- do not reuse Research-use early_access_terms/v1 for Health intake;
- require positive Health classification and governed legal/destination/standing authority;
- respect the ADP provider fingerprint; naming outside a prefix alone is not proof of compatibility;
- declare canonical actor, idempotency namespace, request source and status-recovery consequences;
- re-resolve canonical line fields and prices at the decisive transaction boundary;
- keep raw declared referral separate from canonical sanitized fields and trusted attribution;
- use the existing compatible outbox obligation/renderer design;
- keep unknown-price semantics and current canonical quantity authority; subscription's 50-unit limit is not automatically Health intake policy;
- do not invent the unresolved durable revision/currentness authority or its write protocol.

The commit RPC requires an independently reviewed authority design and exact source scope before implementation. Permission for companion/replay/verifier drafting does not automatically cover it. Existing reader, service, shared and notification edits require their separately allowed diffs. No SQL execution, registration or hosted apply follows from source-drafting permission.

## Customer experience target

When integrations become authorized, finish a native Xenios Health flow, not a second demo:
Products -> customer details -> referral/affiliation -> review -> reference after durable commit.

Use canonical catalog, sessions, published applicable agreements, request persistence and operator workflow. No copied product list, false price, invented offer, duplicate order ledger or optimistic success. Required referral and affiliation answers must allow truthful direct/no-referrer and no-affiliation cases. Keep PII memory-only unless an approved secure draft exists.

Preserve the approved public shell, black rectangular primary controls, outlined secondary controls, solid purple focus, restrained teal, proper labels and error focus. Reuse accepted media behavior; imagery never changes eligibility. Do not rebrand the site or change pricing to make it look complete.

A functioning request flow means an authorized operator can read the exact persisted request/evidence and a retry cannot create a second one. An unavailable panel is useful containment, not completion.

## Compute, testing and handoff

Use one coordinator-granted local slot. Fresh precheck immediately before each process is mandatory. Follow the recorded per-job threshold, no threshold reductions or blind retry. Do not borrow a reviewer's lower-resource run as your qualification.

Run targeted suites first, then broader affected suites/typecheck/build/browser only with their own valid slots. Do not start unauthorized database work. No dependency upgrades or shared configuration changes during this sprint.

Record exact runtime SHA/tree, test SHA, command, toolchain, source-binding scope, result/exit, log hashes and resource receipt. New receipts should expose per-case results. Preserve failures and NOT RUN states. Do not add overlapping counts.

Submit:
- exact source and evidence/handoff identities;
- concrete issue closures and diff;
- red/green tests and boundaries proved;
- protected/manifest/SQL invariance;
- current proposed mount hash and unchanged pending authority;
- no new location violations;
- next dependency-ready authorized action or exact blocker.

No managed writes, real intake, customer data, live email, charges, provider calls, commission, payout, publication or production deployment.

# EXISTING CLAUDE REVIEWER: CONTINUOUS TARGETED ACCEPTANCE

## Role

Remain the single independent acceptance reviewer for the Xenios website. Use the user's Fable 5.1 / Ultracode / highest available setting, but record what the environment actually reports. If requested max and observed xhigh differ, say so. Do not change models or settings in another running session.

Continue your existing context and review branch. Do not restart docs 36/37, duplicate the completed twelve-agent workflow or become the production implementation writer. Specialist review contributions feed your single acceptance record.

This prompt accelerates the review loop. It does not grant founder approvals, source exceptions, managed execution or deployment.

## Anchors

Repository: teamxenios/xenios-website.
Accepted integration: 756a906877dbc174b7e228a259d2faa9c3af48ca, source accepted with release holds in docs 34/35 and correction fffa33a6b3407b407b2b43d3c5a5c7054887f590.
Doc 36: 2d7533f2d3d3a1c69ea686170524d7af4dd6b064.
Doc 37: 324183e886af369a4ea27b9bf0f7b9c615b32139.
Relocated QO source: f1e467f74b01ae2ab866bb791a3c11d657a5d69c.
Tree: 6bc4fd7a7483822d4af87a3c07ab7263c0fbc377.
Records: c807f1913ce95ebcf4113cd4f1ef5bdfb2f45d09.
The same builder already owns the QO-P2-03/04 correction. Obtain its pushed exact successor from the coordinator; do not assume the anchor is still HEAD.

## First review: two HTTP findings and packet delta

Compare the actual successor only against the reviewed relocated source.

QO-P2-03:
- shared/consistent ownership and path derivation;
- case, dot-segment, backslash, encoded segment and slash handling;
- recognized disabled API aliases terminate before body/raw-body parsing;
- expected host normalization is represented rather than guessed;
- no new origin, session or destination authority from URL input.

QO-P2-04:
- unrelated //other and absolute-form non-QO targets call next();
- recognized invalid Quick Order targets remain refused;
- malformed ownership detection does not hijack unrelated root routes;
- no double-next or response-plus-next behavior;
- no security boundary lost to permissive normalization.

Verify packet changes for PWA limitation, regression pins, GATE-01 sequencing, resource provenance and lease hygiene. Verify protected targets, mount application status, SQL and Health gateway/clinical semantics remain unchanged.

Use at most the necessary targeted specialists, ordinarily one HTTP/security reader and one evidence reader. Do not launch a new broad audit unless the actual delta justifies it. A newly discovered material adjacent defect must be reported, not ignored for speed.

## Evidence discipline

Separate:
1. immutable Git identity and diff proof;
2. producer executions you verified from receipts;
3. your own independently executed tests;
4. narrative claims lacking raw provenance;
5. missing qualification.

The reported 73 Node / 116 Vitest runs in docs 36/37 remain historical reviewer evidence, not proof of a new successor or automatic coordinator resource compliance. Current coordinator records identify missing Node wrapper fields and insufficient recorded Vitest headroom against its slot rule. Preserve useful evidence and the limits; do not erase results or fabricate missing attestation.

If new producer receipts accurately bind the changed source and answer the review question, inspect them rather than rerunning everything solely to say you ran it. Independently execute targeted high-risk cases only with a valid shared compute reservation. Do not run concurrently with the builder's heavy process.

A focused pass does not prove typecheck/build/full-App/database. A noindex response is not an access-control proof. A scratchpad patch application is not an authorized production-source edit. Source acceptance is not live intake or release readiness.

## Keep review and repair flowing

At each checkpoint:
- verify exact SHA/tree and relevant baseline;
- identify all material issues in that bounded delta before returning it;
- distinguish regression, carried dependency and nonblocking polish;
- give the smallest coherent repair with exact expected evidence;
- retain acceptance of unchanged reviewed bytes;
- return a durable verdict so the coordinator can schedule the next lawful task.

Do not ask Samuel to resend repository history or arbitrate ordinary CSS and code-style choices already governed by A-E/S1-S7. Do not issue competing approval records. Never speak as Samuel, enter "I approve" on his behalf or accept a generated approval template as an actual owner decision.

Approved communication uses only verified destinations and permitted content. If an outbound tool is denied, do not route around it; return the report in this session and the approved review repository so the authorized coordinator can read it.

## Later mount and persistence reviews

A1 remains a pending exact-baseline protected-edit decision. Review the latest actual proposal, not the held 6481c2ad patch. Current proposed hash at the anchor is c65d7e49a9f5ec87262d4e3b106ab5e16b1c3d1ecd46a01c8a7ca4699e6d92af.

Confirm:
- HARD tracking/attribution effects fully disclosed;
- restricted App/server seam changes and GATE-01 sequencing explicit;
- required positive/negative path/privacy/route/document tests included in the planned authorized slice;
- PWA install-overlay limitation and separate protected scope explicit;
- /health exact gateway preserved, intake has its own predicate;
- applying source, approving successor hashes and updating the manifest are not conflated.

A2 remains pending. When actual drafting permission arrives, review only its exact subset using doc 36 section 7. Do not approve Research-use terms as Health terms. Require explicit positive classification, standing/currentness authority, canonical actor/source/line/quantity and attribution mapping, compatible outbox, complete predecessor anchors and provider-fingerprint compatibility. New object names alone do not prove the ADP fence is safe. Do not permit an unscoped durable revision-authority object or commit RPC to appear under a narrower companion/replay permission.

No local SQL execution is authorized merely by permission to draft. Managed registration/apply and clinical/privacy approval remain separate.

## Whole-site review without reopening the world

After an accepted QO slice and when the coordinator provides the next exact candidate, inspect only newly composed source and affected journeys:
- premium public shell and accessible navigation;
- canonical products, safe media fallback and truthful unavailable states;
- account/partner return and denial;
- Quick Order path ownership/privacy/request boundary;
- operator visibility when implemented;
- subscription disabled purchase boundary.

Use actual production-built client evidence when available. Label fixtures and synthetic accounts. Measure viewport widths, zoom and layout shifts only if actually executed. Do not turn screenshots into proof of real auth, real persistence or payment.

Keep the six real-subscription buying gaps OPEN until independently closed: durable create idempotency, subscription referral lineage, decisive current-price validation, canonical offer projection, durable activation/currentness, independent payment/finality. Preserve PS-R2/PS-R3, MC-01 database/adoption history, D/E reader/writer/delivery/schema, Finance and original protection holds.

## Verdict format

Return:
- exact source/tree and reviewed delta;
- SOURCE: ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH LIMITS / REJECT;
- QO-P2-03 and QO-P2-04: CLOSED / PARTIAL / OPEN;
- invariant and proposal status;
- executed, receipt-verified, narrative-only and missing evidence;
- new findings and the smallest next repair;
- next action permitted under existing scope;
- held founder and hosted decisions.

Use separate final statuses for source integration, live intake, live purchase and production release. Do not grant readiness merely because the sprint window ends.

Then continue with the next actually queued exact review in the active session. If none exists, checkpoint instead of spinning a watcher, inventing a task or claiming perpetual background work.
